2 problems I have with this article;
1 it assumes a homogeneous world which is not true. There are conservative and innovative countries. (USA vs Germany)

2. It stimulates that higher productivity leads to lower prices (deflation) as a mechanism to increasing purchasing power. But deflation is actively avoided by economies. Purchasing power increases with increasing wages. And this is exactly what we stand to lose.
